# What `vercel deploy` (the Vercel CLI) must not upload from this checkout. The demo is built from
# GitHub, where none of these exist: each is git-ignored. The CLI does not read .gitignore, and its
# own short list (node_modules, .venv, .vercel, .env.local, ...) would still send backend/.env,
# with your OpenAI key and read-write DATABASE_URL, which the function would then read, and the
# local vector store and models. Each line repeats a .gitignore rule, so nothing a push holds is
# left out; backend/tests/test_vercel.py checks that against the files the API needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/.venv/
*.egg-info/
data/chroma/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep
data/external/
data/models/
data/stance/
data/eval_cache/
deploy/build/
